{"sourceSha256": "3990145be894007d26b59f11ab007a622474d495eb8ba7621663fd09efb20464", "text": "82 Logan Road\nAscot, Qid 4542\n\nFAV /2019\n\nDear Doctor,\nRe: Andrew Smith, DOB 15/09/19\n\n| am writing to request urgent assessment for Andrew, a two- month- old boy who has been\ndiagnosed with infantile hypertrophic-pylonic stenosis (IHPS) as confirmed by ultrasound.\n\nHis symptoms initially appeared two days ago when he presented with a history of crying\nspells and vomiting while eating. His examination revealed a decrease in his body weight\ncompared to his previous six week routine check-up, but he was well hydrated. His test\nfeeding showed visible stomach contractions along with a palpable olive like mass.\nTherefore, an ultrasound was ordered to rule out IHPS.\n\nToday on his review Andrew’s condition has continued to deteriorate. His vomiting has\npersisted anc a mild dehydration was noticed. The ultrasound revealed a thick pyloric\n\nmuscle.\n\nIn regards to his birth history, he ts the first baby of his parents. His perinatal history is\nnormal and he was born vaginally with a birth weight of 2750 grams, which had increased to\n3050 grams on his six week follow-up.\n\n| would be grateful if you could start intravenous fluids for the dehydration and assess his\n\ncondition for possible surgery. Please do not hesitate to contact me if you have any quenes.", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "82 Logan Road\nAscot, Qid 4542\n\nFAV /2019\n\nDear Doctor,\nRe: Andrew Smith, DOB 15/09/19\n\n| am writing to request urgent assessment for Andrew, a two- month- old boy who has been\ndiagnosed with infantile hypertrophic-pylonic stenosis (IHPS) as confirmed by ultrasound.\n\nHis symptoms initially appeared two days ago when he presented with a history of crying\nspells and vomiting while eating. His examination revealed a decrease in his body weight\ncompared to his previous six week routine check-up, but he was well hydrated. His test\nfeeding showed visible stomach contractions along with a palpable olive like mass.\nTherefore, an ultrasound was ordered to rule out IHPS.\n\nToday on his review Andrew’s condition has continued to deteriorate. His vomiting has\npersisted anc a mild dehydration was noticed. The ultrasound revealed a thick pyloric\n\nmuscle.\n\nIn regards to his birth history, he ts the first baby of his parents. His perinatal history is\nnormal and he was born vaginally with a birth weight of 2750 grams, which had increased to\n3050 grams on his six week follow-up.\n\n| would be grateful if you could start intravenous fluids for the dehydration and assess his\n\ncondition for possible surgery. Please do not hesitate to contact me if you have any quenes.", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2180.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "82 Logan Road\nAscot, Qid 4542", "lines": [{"text": "82 Logan Road", "x": 0.00367, "y": 0.0, "width": 0.1578, "height": 0.02679, "confidence": 0.963, "words": [{"text": "82", "x": 0.00367, "width": 0.02615, "confidence": 0.962}, {"text": "Logan", "x": 0.04083, "width": 0.0578, "confidence": 0.962}, {"text": "Road", "x": 0.10963, "width": 0.05183, "confidence": 0.966}], "uncertainWords": []}, {"text": "Ascot, Qid 4542", "x": 0.00459, "y": 0.03929, "width": 0.16927, "height": 0.0275, "confidence": 0.916, "words": [{"text": "Ascot,", "x": 0.00459, "width": 0.16927, "confidence": 0.933}, {"text": "Qid", "x": 0.08211, "width": 0.03257, "confidence": 0.844}, {"text": "4542", "x": 0.12615, "width": 0.04771, "confidence": 0.97}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "FAV /2019", "lines": [{"text": "FAV /2019", "x": 0.0055, "y": 0.10107, "width": 0.11422, "height": 0.01357, "confidence": 0.0, "words": [{"text": "FAV", "x": 0.0055, "width": 0.04679, "confidence": 0.0}, {"text": "/2019", "x": 0.05872, "width": 0.06101, "confidence": 0.0}], "uncertainWords": ["FAV", "/2019"]}]}, {"text": "Dear Doctor,\nRe: Andrew Smith, DOB 15/09/19", "lines": [{"text": "Dear Doctor,", "x": 0.006